1
00:00:00,180 --> 00:00:01,200
(Priya:)Mmm, me, too.

2
00:00:01,200 --> 00:00:02,710
You know, I was thinking:

3
00:00:02,720 --> 00:00:05,630
(Leonard:)There are some great
research facilities in India.

4
00:00:05,630 --> 00:00:08,440
(Priya:)Where are you going
with this, Leonard?

5
00:00:08,440 --> 00:00:12,190
Well, I'm just saying, you know,
I don't have any real ties here,

6
00:00:12,190 --> 00:00:15,410
(Leonard:)so if I were to move to New
Delhi, we could, you know--

7
00:00:15,410 --> 00:00:18,280
(Leonard:)go out.

8
00:00:18,280 --> 00:00:21,920
(Priya:)Leonard, didn't we have this
conversation five years ago?

9
00:00:21,920 --> 00:00:22,880
(Leonard:)Well, yes, but...

10
00:00:22,890 --> 00:00:24,120
(Leonard:)things have changed.

11
00:00:24,120 --> 00:00:25,720
(Leonard:)You know, you're older,
I'm older--

12
00:00:25,720 --> 00:00:27,910
(Leonard:)Look, no more
superhero bed sheets.

13
00:00:27,910 --> 00:00:29,370
(Priya:)Sweetheart,

14
00:00:29,380 --> 00:00:32,380
(Priya:)just because we have fun when
I come to town doesn't mean

15
00:00:32,380 --> 00:00:35,000
(Priya:)I want to have a
serious relationship.

16
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:35,960
(Leonard:)It doesn't?

17
00:00:35,970 --> 00:00:37,370
(Priya:)Mm-mm.

18
00:00:37,370 --> 00:00:40,640
(Priya:)And besides, I could never bring
a white boy home to my parents.

19
00:00:41,540 --> 00:00:42,700
(Priya:)They'd have a cow.

20
00:00:42,710 --> 00:00:45,340
(Priya:)Which is a much
bigger deal in India.

21
00:00:45,340 --> 00:00:47,780
(Leonard:)I'm not that white.

22
00:00:47,780 --> 00:00:49,840
My great-great-grandmother
was half Cherokee.

23
00:00:49,850 --> 00:00:52,910
(Leonard:)I know that's not the right kind
of Indian, but it is something.

24
00:00:52,920 --> 00:00:54,620
(Priya:)You're funny.

25
00:00:54,620 --> 00:00:58,600
(Priya:)Leonard?

26
00:00:59,490 --> 00:01:00,490
(Sheldon:)What?

